150
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:15,240
My treat.

151
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:22,100
So we use this phrase when we want to say I'll invite you, I'll pay for you.

152
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:22,500
I'll pay.

153
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:27,140
Right, so I can say, hey, let's go get some beers.

154
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:28,280
It's my treat.

155
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:29,180
Oh, thanks, Marco.

156
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,440
So I'm paying, right?

157
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:32,760
My treat.

158
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:36,240
And our last phrase for fluency builder.

159
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:37,800
A twist of fate.

160
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,560
So Erica, what is a twist of fate?

161
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:51,820
A twist of fate is an unplanned event that has a big impact on your future or your life.

162
00:07:52,140 --> 00:07:52,500
Okay.

163
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:55,440
Marco, can you give us an example of a twist of fate?

164
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:57,760
All right, for example.

165
00:07:58,220 --> 00:08:02,040
Okay, you're supposed to catch a flight to another country, all right?

166
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,720
But you're late, so you miss your flight.

167
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,360
Okay.

168
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:08,680
And that flight crashes.

169
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,760
Wow.

170
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:12,960
Right, so that's a twist of fate.

171
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:15,680
So yeah, it's like fate, it's like destiny.

172
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,280
You weren't supposed to be on that flight.

173
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,960
Okay, so a twist of fate.

174
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,240
A twist of fate.

175
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,240
Great.

176
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:28,020
